# See https://help.github.com/articles/ignoring-files/ for more about ignoring files.

# ─── Next.js / Node ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
/node_modules
/.pnp
.pnp.*
.yarn/*
!.yarn/patches
!.yarn/plugins
!.yarn/releases
!.yarn/versions
/coverage
/.next/
/out/
/build
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
.pnpm-debug.log*
*.tsbuildinfo
next-env.d.ts
.vercel
.DS_Store
*.pem

# env files
.env*

# ─── .NET / ASP.NET Core ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Build output
GroupBuyingApi/**/bin/
GroupBuyingApi/**/obj/

# Visual Studio files
GroupBuyingApi/**/.vs/
GroupBuyingApi/**/*.user
GroupBuyingApi/**/*.suo

# !! NEVER commit these — they may contain secrets !!
# Production / staging overrides (use env vars on server instead)
GroupBuyingApi/**/appsettings.Production.json
GroupBuyingApi/**/appsettings.Staging.json
GroupBuyingApi/**/appsettings.local.json

# .NET User Secrets are stored in AppData — NOT here — so no ignore rule needed.
# Location: %APPDATA%\Microsoft\UserSecrets\<UserSecretsId>\secrets.json
# Run: dotnet user-secrets list   (to view)
# Run: dotnet user-secrets set    (to add)

# EF Core migrations snapshot (optional — remove if you want to track migrations)
# GroupBuyingApi/**/Migrations/

# Publish output
GroupBuyingApi/**/publish/

# ─── Security Audits (local only — NEVER push to GitHub) ─────────────────────
SECURITY_AUDIT.md
SECURITY_AUDIT*.md
*_audit.md
*_audit_*.md
